ARTICLE 4 — KEY PERSONNEL

4.1 Named Key Personnel. The Contractor shall assign the named Key Personnel in Schedule C, including:

(a) Engagement Director (minimum allocation 25%);

(b) Engagement Manager (minimum allocation 100%);

(c) Lead Solution Architect (minimum allocation 75% Weeks 1-12, then 25% thereafter);

(d) Lead Application Engineer (minimum allocation 100% Weeks 12-44);

(e) Senior Data Migration Engineer (minimum allocation 100% Weeks 16-38);

(f) Accessibility Lead (minimum allocation 50% Weeks 12-40);

(g) Bilingual UX Lead (minimum allocation 75% Weeks 12-40).

4.2 No Replacement Without Consent. The Contractor shall not replace any Key Personnel without the State Agency's prior written consent. The State Agency reserves the right to interview and approve any proposed replacement before the replacement begins work on the Project.

4.3 Background Checks. All Contractor personnel assigned to this Project shall pass the State Agency's background check requirements (Schedule D), which include criminal history checks and may require fingerprint-based checks for personnel with access to State Agency systems containing personal information.

4.4 MWBE Participation. The Contractor shall use commercially reasonable efforts to subcontract to certified Minority and Women-Owned Business Enterprises (MWBEs) consistent with the State Agency's MWBE participation goals set forth in Schedule E. The Contractor shall report MWBE participation quarterly during the Project.

4.5 OFCCP Equal Opportunity. As a contractor providing services to a state agency, the Contractor shall comply with all applicable federal and state equal employment opportunity requirements.

4.6 Removal of Personnel. The State Agency may, at any time and without cause, request that the Contractor remove any individual from the Project. The Contractor shall remove the named individual within five (5) business days.

ARTICLE 4 — KEY PERSONNEL

4.1 Named Key Personnel. The Service Provider shall assign the following individuals as Key Personnel for this Project, each of whom is named in Schedule B:

(a) Engagement Partner (minimum allocation 25% across the Project duration);

(b) Engagement Manager (minimum allocation 100% across the Project duration);

(c) Lead Banking Platform Engineer (minimum allocation 100% across Project Weeks 4 through 22);

(d) Senior Integration Engineer (minimum allocation 100% across Project Weeks 8 through 18);

(e) Senior Dashboard Engineer (minimum allocation 100% across Project Weeks 12 through 20);

(f) Quality Assurance Lead (minimum allocation 100% across Project Weeks 12 through 22).

4.2 No Replacement Without Consent. The Service Provider shall not replace, reassign, or substantially reduce the allocation of any Key Personnel without the Bank's prior written consent (which the Bank may grant or withhold in its reasonable discretion), except in the case of (i) the Key Personnel's resignation from the Service Provider, (ii) termination of the Key Personnel's employment for cause, or (iii) the Key Personnel's death, disability, or extended leave of absence. In any of these cases, the Service Provider shall promptly propose a replacement of comparable skills, experience, and seniority, and the Bank reserves the right to interview and approve the proposed replacement before the replacement begins work on the Project.

4.3 Background Checks and Cleared Personnel. All Service Provider personnel assigned to this Project shall have completed (a) the background investigations required by the MSA, (b) a credit history check consistent with applicable banking regulations on personnel handling sensitive Bank systems, and (c) the Bank's standard security awareness training prior to receiving access to any Bank systems or Bank Materials. Personnel who have not completed these requirements shall not be granted access. The Service Provider shall maintain documentation of personnel clearances and shall make such documentation available to the Bank's vendor risk team upon request.

4.4 Onshore-Only Requirement. All In-Scope Activities shall be performed exclusively from facilities physically located in the contiguous United States, by personnel who are United States citizens or lawful permanent residents physically present in the contiguous United States. The Service Provider shall not, without the Bank's prior written consent (which the Bank may grant or withhold in its sole discretion), perform any In-Scope Activities from, or grant any Service Provider personnel access to Bank Materials or Bank systems from, any location outside of the contiguous United States. This Section is an essential term of this SOW and a material part of the Bank's regulatory posture.

4.5 Removal of Personnel. The Bank may, at any time and without cause, request that the Service Provider remove any individual from the Project. The Service Provider shall, within five (5) business days following receipt of such request, remove the named individual from the Project and propose a replacement.

4.6 Non-Solicitation. The Service Provider shall not, during the Project Period and for twelve (12) months following the Project End Date, solicit for employment any Bank employee with whom the Service Provider personnel had material contact during the Project, subject to the customary general-solicitation carve-out in the MSA.

ARTICLE 4 — KEY PERSONNEL

4.1 Named Key Personnel. The Provider shall assign the following individuals as Key Personnel for this Project, each of whom is named in Schedule C together with such individual's role, expected minimum allocation percentage, and the period during which such individual is expected to be allocated to the Project:

(a) Engineering Lead (minimum allocation 100% across the entire Project Period);

(b) Principal Architect (minimum allocation 75% during Project Weeks 1 through 14, 25% thereafter);

(c) Senior Software Engineer — Posting Engine (minimum allocation 100% during Project Weeks 6 through 24);

(d) Senior Software Engineer — Integration Layer (minimum allocation 100% during Project Weeks 10 through 32);

(e) Senior Software Engineer — Reporting Feeds (minimum allocation 100% during Project Weeks 14 through 38);

(f) Quality Assurance Lead (minimum allocation 100% during Project Weeks 14 through 44);

(g) Application Security Lead (minimum allocation 50% during Project Weeks 6 through 40).

4.2 No Replacement Without Consent. The Provider shall not replace, reassign, or substantially reduce the allocation of any Key Personnel without the Client's prior written consent (which consent shall not be unreasonably withheld), except in the case of (i) the Key Personnel's resignation from the Provider, (ii) termination of the Key Personnel's employment for cause, (iii) the Key Personnel's death, disability, or extended leave of absence, or (iv) the Client's request for removal under Section 4.4.

4.3 Background Checks and Training. All Provider personnel assigned to this Project shall have completed the background investigations and security training required by the MSA prior to receiving access to any Client systems or Client Materials. The Background investigation shall include credit history verification (consistent with applicable banking regulations on personnel handling sensitive systems).

4.4 Removal of Personnel. The Client may, at any time and without cause, request that the Provider remove any individual from the Project. The Provider shall, within ten (10) business days following receipt of such request, remove the named individual from the Project and propose a replacement of comparable skills, experience, and seniority.

4.5 Non-Solicitation of Key Personnel. During the Project Period and for twelve (12) months following the Project End Date, neither Party shall solicit for employment any Key Personnel of the other Party who is materially involved in this Project, subject to the customary general-solicitation carve-out in the MSA.
